    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW266b2wAzfAJMBjD5JpGuLWE)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent; builds on #499 and #501 (both merged).\n\n## What changes\n\n- Both keys act only while DEVONthink is in front (the hotkeys are switched on and off by an app watcher).\n- `Cmd+Z`: runs Edit > Undo only when its title says highlight, annotation or markup (e.g. \"Undo Add Highlight\"). Otherwise the normal Cmd+Z goes to DEVONthink.\n- No stale highlights: the Edit menu always shows the next undo step. A highlight that is gone, or that came before another action, is not touched.\n- `Cmd+Shift+D`: runs View > \"Hide Inspector\" or \"Hide Sidebar\" when one is shown. Otherwise the normal Cmd+Shift+D goes to DEVONthink.\n- `DEVONthink.dumpMenu(\"Edit\")` in the Hammerspoon console prints a menu's titles, to fix the patterns if needed.\n\n## Things to check\n\n- I could not read DEVONthink's menus from here, so the title patterns are a best guess.\n- Cmd+Shift+D may already be a DEVONthink shortcut. While the sidebar is shown, this PR overrides it. Check Edit/View/Go/Tools in DEVONthink for it.\n- If DEVONthink does not put highlights on the undo stack, Cmd+Z will pass through unchanged and nothing is deleted. Tell me the Edit menu text after making a highlight.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Reload Hammerspoon: no error in the console.\n- [ ] Make a highlight (Caps+x, then select text), open the Edit menu: note the Undo title.\n- [ ] Press Cmd+Z: the highlight disappears.\n- [ ] Press Cmd+Z again with no highlight to undo: normal DEVONthink undo behaviour, no error.\n- [ ] Make a highlight, then another action (e.g. rename an item), press Cmd+Z: the rename is undone, the highlight stays.\n- [ ] Show the inspector/sidebar, press Cmd+Shift+D: it closes.\n- [ ] Press Cmd+Shift+D with both hidden: DEVONthink's own Cmd+Shift+D behaviour, if any.\n- [ ] In another app (e.g. Emacs, Finder), Cmd+Z and Cmd+Shift+D behave as usual.\n- [ ] Caps+x and Caps+c still work.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCTb5QFPFZUd9wzRgq)_",
